ps://api.github.com/repos/SaiSamyukthVemuri/Hone/actions/runs/36865894273/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SaiSamyukthVemuri/Hone/actions/workflows/289443461","head_commit":{"id":"7d25459de1fe63a7fd4ed3348ecb11ab35ab6338","tree_id":"bbbb9c830c3e94b4a3eb826c3f3eac2b3fe37a2d","message":"feat(ui): UX-02 slice 3 — finish SectionLabel adoption across session charting\n\n`components/ui/section-label.tsx` owns the uppercase section label. Thirteen\ncall sites across the session-charting directory spelled its class list out by\nhand; this slice replaces them with the primitive and retires their baseline\nentries. The remaining census goes 69 -> 56.\n\nScope was DERIVED, not chosen. The population comes from the guard's own\npredicate read out of the primitive — typography, exactly one contract size, a\nmuted tone, and nothing else — so every converted site was already proved to\ncarry no information the primitive lacks. The directory holds thirteen `.tsx`\nfiles and the other eight contain no `uppercase` at all, which is what makes\nthese five the whole surface rather than a subset.\n\nWHY THIS SURFACE. It is the only remaining candidate that reaches zero of BOTH\ndetector shapes: no exact duplicates and no layout-decorated ones. Calendar\nholds the larger population (23) and cannot finish — two decorated labels stay\nbehind in `calendar/[id]/page.tsx` — and it is baselined T2, which buys a\nheavier lane than a label swap needs. A `components/**` slice pulls the payment\nlane on one filename and has a `<label>` host the primitive's `as=` union does\nnot cover. This diff is T1, lanes application + browser_core.\n\nEQUIVALENCE, stated precisely. Every host tag is preserved via `as=`; there is\nno `<div>` in the population, so nothing moves between block and inline, and no\nsite carried an attribute beyond `className`. `text-neutral-500` becomes the\nprimitive's `text-fg-muted`: `--color-fg-muted` is `oklch(55.6% 0 0)`, defined\nexactly once, and Hone's `dark` variant maps to a `.dark` class that is never\napplied — so the computed colour is identical in every reachable theme. The\nclass STRING does change, so the guard's claims are about adoption and the\nabsence of duplicates, never about byte-identical output.\n\nBaseline entries are DELETED rather than commented out. Rule 3a-bis exists\nbecause a surviving entry keeps its allowance: a stub saying \"this path may hold\nN\" would let every retired duplicate return and still pass.\n\nThe table's ownership note is removed rather than refreshed. It attributed two\nfiles to another open PR, that attribution had already gone stale, and a count\ntable is the wrong place to track branch state.\n\nVerification: guard 26/26; both halves proved non-vacuous by mutation — a\nreintroduced duplicate reds rule 2, and restoring a retired entry reds rule 3a;\n`tsc --noEmit` clean; 57 affected test files, 1041 tests pass; lint introduces\nzero new messages, confirmed by linting the base content of the two files that\ncarry pre-existing unused-var warnings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:01:17Z","author":{"name":"SaiSamyukthVemuri","email":"samyukth.ssv@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"SaiSamyukthVemuri","email":"samyukth.ssv@gmail.com"}},"repository":{"id":1240764106,"node_id":"R_kgDOSfSOyg","name":"Hone","full_name":"SaiSamyukthVemuri/Hone","private":false,"owner":{"login":"SaiSamyukthVemuri","id":26781116,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzgxMTE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26781116?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaiSamyukthVemuri","html_url":"https://github.com/SaiSamyukthVemuri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaiSamyukthVemuri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaiSamyukthVemuri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaiSamyukthVemuri/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.git